  var approvedGuides = {"/food-and-drink/reel-plaice-ayr":"<h2>A fish-supper stop in Ayr</h2>\n<p>Fish and chips, a bit of sea air and time for a wander — now that’s a lovely way to spend a day in Ayr. Reel Plaice is a fish-and-chip stop at 22 Bath Place, close enough to work into a seafront outing. Tripadvisor diners mention fish cooked to order, the batter and the welcome. Have a look at their accounts, choose what suits your group and give lunch a proper place in the day.</p>\n<h2>Make room for the seafront</h2>\n<p>Ayr’s beach gives you something to do either side of lunch. The esplanade follows the shore from the harbour towards the River Doon, while the Low Green provides open space for a slower stop by the sea. You can make this a simple wander and food outing without booking a packed afternoon of attractions.</p>\n<p>For a relaxed plan, explore the waterfront first, decide how far your group wants to walk and leave the food stop as a proper break. If the weather turns, shorten the walk rather than forcing a full route. Check the council’s beach information before making swimming part of the day.</p>\n<h2>Add a different kind of discovery</h2>\n<p>If you want more than a beach walk, the <a href=\"/museums/robert-burns-birthplace-museum/ayr\">Robert Burns Birthplace Museum</a> in Alloway adds a literary and heritage stop. The National Trust for Scotland’s site includes Burns Cottage and a museum collection connected with the poet’s life.</p>\n<p>Alloway is south of Ayr, so plan it as another stop with its own journey time. Check admission, opening times and access details before committing to both the museum and a meal. The <a href=\"/destination/ayr\">Ayr destination guide</a> brings other options together if you would rather stay closer to town.</p>\n<h2>Before you visit Reel Plaice</h2>\n<p>Call 01292 431535 for the current opening hours, menu and service arrangements. Ask directly about seating, takeaway service and any dietary requirements that matter to your group. The customer-review link is useful for other diners’ experiences; it is separate from a current menu or a booking service.</p>\n<p>Use the directions link for 22 Bath Place, Ayr, KA7 1DP. Decide how the meal fits around parking or your train journey, and leave enough time to enjoy it. A food stop should make the day easier, not send everyone rushing across town.</p>\n<h2>Guide sources</h2>\n<p>Venue information and customer feedback: <a href=\"https://www.tripadvisor.co.uk/Restaurant_Review-g186574-d27929163-Reviews-Reel_Plaice-Ayr_South_Ayrshire_Ayrshire_Scotland.html\">Tripadvisor’s Reel Plaice listing</a>. Seafront context: <a href=\"https://destinationsouthayrshire.co.uk/things-to-do/ayr-beach/\">Destination South Ayrshire</a>. Museum and travel information: <a href=\"https://www.nts.org.uk/visit/places/robert-burns-birthplace-museum/planning-your-visit\">National Trust for Scotland</a>.</p>\n"};
